module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.TensorProduct.Quotient
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Branches.Completion
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Etale.IndEtaleUniverse
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Henselian.StrictHenselization.Quotient
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.LocalRing.CotangentQuotient

/-!
# Henselization is compatible with quotients, with the base and the henselization in
independent universes

Let `(R, 𝔪, κ)` be a local ring, let `Rh` be a henselization of `R` and let `I ⊆ 𝔪` be an ideal.
Stacks 05WQ says that `Rh/I Rh` is a henselization of `R/I`. `IsLocalRing.henselization_quotient`
proves it for `R` and `Rh` in **one** universe, spelling "is a henselization" as the four-item
package of Lemma 04GN. The same statement is proved here for the predicate
`IsLocalRing.IsHenselization`, whose three universes — base, prescribed residue extension and
henselization — are independent.

The universe gap is not idle. The henselian local ring `𝒪^h_{X, x}` of a decent algebraic space
at a point (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.henselianLocalRing`) is a colimit indexed by the category of
elementary étale neighbourhoods, so it is a ring in `Type (u + 1)`, while the Zariski local ring
`𝒪_{U, u}` of a chart of which it is a henselization
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.henselianLocalRing_isHenselization`) is a ring in `Type u`. The
same-universe form of Stacks 05WQ therefore does not apply to it at all.

## Main results

* `IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.indEtale_quotient`: the quotient of a henselization by the ideal
  generated by an ideal of the base is ind-étale over the quotient of the base, with the two
  universes independent. This is the only conjunct of Stacks 05WQ that is universe-sensitive.
* `IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.of_ringEquiv_base`: being a henselization transports along a ring
  isomorphism of the base, the prescribed residue extension travelling with it.
* `IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.quotient_of_le_maximalIdeal`: Stacks 05WQ for
  `IsLocalRing.IsHenselization`, with the base and the henselization in independent universes.
* `IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.exists_ringEquiv_quotient_algebraMap_of_isHenselization`: the
  form the geometry needs. If `A` is a quotient of `R` and `H` is a henselization of `A`, then
  `H` is isomorphic, as a ring, to `Rh/I Rh` for `I` the kernel of `R → A`, **by an isomorphism
  carrying the class of `algebraMap R Rh r` to `algebraMap A H (algebraMap R A r)`**. The three
  rings `R`, `Rh` and `H` are in three independent universes.
* `IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.exists_ringEquiv_quotient_of_isHenselization`: the same with that
  compatibility forgotten.

## Implementation notes

*Which conjunct needs the universes.* Of the three fields of `IsLocalRing.IsHenselization`, two
are already universe-free: henselianness of `Rh/I Rh` is
`Stacks.Henselian.henselianLocalRing_quotient`, and the residue-field conjunct is obtained by
composing three isomorphisms of residue fields, two of them along the surjections `R → R/I` and
`Rh → Rh/I Rh`
(`Stacks.StrictHenselization.QuotientDescent.residueField_map_bijective_of_surjective`) and
the third the one carried by the henselization. Only ind-étaleness is stated in a category
`CommAlgCat.{·} ·` that holds algebras of one size, and for it the universe-free form
`StacksDraft.IndEtale` and its cobase change `StacksDraft.indEtale_tensorProduct` are available;
the quotient is matched with the tensor product by
`Algebra.TensorProduct.quotIdealMapEquivQuotTensor`. So no `ULift` repackaging of
`IsLocalRing.henselization_quotient` is needed, and none is done.

*The prescribed residue extension.* The hypothesis of `quotient_of_le_maximalIdeal` is that `Rh`
is a henselization of `R` with respect to `κ` itself, which is Stacks 05WQ; the conclusion is
that `Rh/I Rh` is one of `R/I` with respect to `κ(R/I)`, again the source's. This is what makes
the conclusion usable with the uniqueness of Lemma 08HT against another henselization of `R/I`,
which also carries `κ(R/I)`: the comparison needs the two prescribed extensions to agree, and
`AlgEquiv.refl` then serves. The strict analogue, with `L` a separable algebraic closure of `κ`
and the target's own residue field prescribed, is `IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.quotient`
(Stacks 05WS), and it is stated for `R` and `Rh` in one universe.

*`of_ringEquiv_base` against `residueField_of_ringEquiv`.* Both move the base of a henselization
along a ring isomorphism. `IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.residueField_of_ringEquiv` prescribes the
*target's* residue field in its conclusion, which discards the identification of the base's
residue field with the prescribed extension; `of_ringEquiv_base` keeps the base's own residue
field, transporting it along the isomorphism, and that is what a Lemma 08HT comparison at
`κ(base)` needs.

*`IsHenselization` is not weakened into an argument.*
`exists_ringEquiv_quotient_of_isHenselization` takes `A` as an arbitrary quotient of `R`,
presented by a surjection rather than as `R ⧸ I`, so that no instance of `IsLocalRing (R ⧸ I)`
has to be bound ahead of the later binders; `I` is read off as the kernel. `I ≤ 𝔪` is then
automatic, a kernel of a map to a nontrivial ring being proper.

## References

* [StacksProject 05WQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05WQ)
* [StacksProject 04GQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04GQ), the predicate
  `IsLocalRing.IsHenselization`
* [StacksProject 08HT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08HT), the uniqueness of the
  henselization
* [StacksProject 0BSH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BSH), stability of ind-étale under
  cobase change
* [StacksProject 0EMY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EMY), the henselian local ring of a
  decent algebraic space as a henselization of a chart stalk, which is where the universe gap
  comes from
-/

@[expose] public section

open IsLocalRing
open scoped TensorProduct

universe u v w x

namespace IsLocalRing.IsHenselization

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    {Rh : Type w} [CommRing Rh] [IsLocalRing Rh] [Algebra R Rh]

/-- **The quotient of a henselization is ind-étale over the quotient of the base**, with the base
and the henselization in independent universes.

`Rh/I Rh` is the cobase change `(R/I) ⊗_R Rh` of the ind-étale `R`-algebra `Rh`
(`Algebra.TensorProduct.quotIdealMapEquivQuotTensor`), and ind-étaleness is stable under cobase
change by Stacks 0BSH, in the universe-free form `StacksDraft.indEtale_tensorProduct`. -/
theorem indEtale_quotient {L : Type v} [Field L] [Algebra (ResidueField R) L]
    [IsHenselization R L Rh] (I : Ideal R) :
    StacksDraft.IndEtale (R ⧸ I) (Rh ⧸ I.map (algebraMap R Rh)) :=
  StacksDraft.indEtale_of_equiv (RingEquiv.refl (R ⧸ I))
    (Algebra.TensorProduct.quotIdealMapEquivQuotTensor Rh I).symm.toRingEquiv
    (fun a ↦ (Algebra.TensorProduct.quotIdealMapEquivQuotTensor Rh I).symm.commutes a)
    (StacksDraft.indEtale_tensorProduct (R ⧸ I) (ind_etale (R := R) (L := L) (Rh := Rh)))

/-- **Being a henselization transports along a ring isomorphism of the base.** If `Rh` is a
henselization of `R` with respect to `κ(R)` and `σ : R' ≃+* R` is compatible with the structure
maps, then `Rh` is a henselization of `R'` with respect to `κ(R')`.

Unlike `IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.residueField_of_ringEquiv`, which concludes with the residue
field of `Rh` prescribed, the prescribed extension travels along `σ`: the identification of
`κ(R')` with the residue field of `Rh` is the one carried by the henselization conjugated by
`IsLocalRing.ResidueField.mapEquiv σ`. -/
theorem of_ringEquiv_base [IsHenselization R (ResidueField R) Rh]
    {R' : Type v} [CommRing R'] [IsLocalRing R'] [Algebra R' Rh] (σ : R' ≃+* R)
    (hσ : ∀ r, algebraMap R' Rh r = algebraMap R Rh (σ r)) :
    IsHenselization R' (ResidueField R') Rh := by
  refine ⟨henselian (R := R) (L := ResidueField R) (Rh := Rh),
    StacksDraft.indEtale_of_equiv σ.symm (RingEquiv.refl Rh)
      (fun a ↦ by rw [hσ, σ.apply_symm_apply]; rfl)
      (ind_etale (R := R) (L := ResidueField R) (Rh := Rh)), ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := exists_residueFieldEquiv (R := R) (L := ResidueField R) (Rh := Rh)
  refine ⟨(ResidueField.mapEquiv σ).trans e, fun r ↦ ?_⟩
  have hres : ResidueField.mapEquiv σ (residue R' r) = residue R (σ r) :=
    ResidueField.map_residue (σ : R' →+* R) r
  simp only [Algebra.algebraMap_self, RingHom.id_apply, RingEquiv.coe_trans,
    Function.comp_apply, hres]
  rw [hσ r]
  simpa only [Algebra.algebraMap_self, RingHom.id_apply] using he (σ r)

open Stacks.StrictHenselization.QuotientDescent in
/-- **Henselization is compatible with quotients** (Stacks 05WQ), with the base and the
henselization in independent universes. Let `(R, 𝔪, κ)` be a local ring, let `Rh` be a
henselization of `R` and let `I ⊆ 𝔪` be an ideal. Then `Rh/I Rh` is a henselization of `R/I`,
with respect to the residue field of `R/I`.

`Rh/I Rh` is henselian because a quotient of a henselian local ring by a proper ideal is
(`Stacks.Henselian.henselianLocalRing_quotient`); it is ind-étale over `R/I` by
`IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.indEtale_quotient`; and its residue field is that of `R/I` because
the two quotient maps `R → R/I` and `Rh → Rh/I Rh` are surjective local maps, hence
isomorphisms on residue fields, and the third side of the square is the identification carried by
the henselization. -/
@[stacks 05WQ "`R^h` is the henselization of `R` in the sense of Definition 04GQ (1),
`IsHenselization R (ResidueField R) Rh`, which by Lemma 04GN exists and by Lemma 08HT is unique
up to unique isomorphism over `R`; the conclusion says that `R^h/IR^h` is the henselization of
`R/I` in the same sense, `IsHenselization (R ⧸ I) (ResidueField (R ⧸ I)) (Rh ⧸ I.map (algebraMap
R Rh))`, for the `R/I`-algebra structure induced by `R → R^h`. The locality of the two quotients
follows from `I ⊆ 𝔪` and is supplied in the statement. The base and the henselization live in
independent universes."]
theorem quotient_of_le_maximalIdeal [IsHenselization R (ResidueField R) Rh]
    {I : Ideal R} (hI : I ≤ maximalIdeal R) :
    letI : IsLocalRing (R ⧸ I) := isLocalRing_quotient_of_le_maximalIdeal I hI
    letI : IsLocalRing (Rh ⧸ I.map (algebraMap R Rh)) :=
      isLocalRing_quotient_of_le_maximalIdeal (I.map (algebraMap R Rh))
        ((Ideal.map_mono hI).trans (map_maximalIdeal (R := R) (L := ResidueField R)).le)
    IsHenselization (R ⧸ I) (ResidueField (R ⧸ I)) (Rh ⧸ I.map (algebraMap R Rh)) := by
  have hJ : I.map (algebraMap R Rh) ≤ maximalIdeal Rh :=
    (Ideal.map_mono hI).trans (map_maximalIdeal (R := R) (L := ResidueField R)).le
  let : IsLocalRing (R ⧸ I) := isLocalRing_quotient_of_le_maximalIdeal I hI
  let : IsLocalRing (Rh ⧸ I.map (algebraMap R Rh)) :=
    isLocalRing_quotient_of_le_maximalIdeal (I.map (algebraMap R Rh)) hJ
  have hJne : I.map (algebraMap R Rh) ≠ ⊤ := fun h ↦
    (maximalIdeal.isMaximal Rh).ne_top (top_le_iff.mp (h ▸ hJ))
  have hhens : HenselianLocalRing Rh := henselian (R := R) (L := ResidueField R) (Rh := Rh)
  have hsurjR : Function.Surjective (algebraMap R (R ⧸ I)) :=
    surjective_algebraMap_quotient I
  have hsurjRh : Function.Surjective (algebraMap Rh (Rh ⧸ I.map (algebraMap R Rh))) :=
    surjective_algebraMap_quotient (I.map (algebraMap R Rh))
  have : IsLocalHom (algebraMap R (R ⧸ I)) := IsLocalHom.of_surjective _ hsurjR
  have : IsLocalHom (algebraMap Rh (Rh ⧸ I.map (algebraMap R Rh))) :=
    IsLocalHom.of_surjective _ hsurjRh
  have hbijR := residueField_map_bijective_of_surjective (algebraMap R (R ⧸ I)) hsurjR
  have hbijRh := residueField_map_bijective_of_surjective
    (algebraMap Rh (Rh ⧸ I.map (algebraMap R Rh))) hsurjRh
  obtain ⟨e₀, he₀⟩ := exists_residueFieldEquiv (R := R) (L := ResidueField R) (Rh := Rh)
  have he₀' : ∀ r : R, e₀ (residue R r) = residue Rh (algebraMap R Rh r) := fun r ↦ by
    simpa only [Algebra.algebraMap_self, RingHom.id_apply] using he₀ r
  refine ⟨Stacks.Henselian.henselianLocalRing_quotient hJne,
    indEtale_quotient (L := ResidueField R) I, ?_⟩
  refine ⟨((RingEquiv.ofBijective _ hbijR).symm.trans e₀).trans
    (RingEquiv.ofBijective _ hbijRh), fun y ↦ ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨r, rfl⟩ := hsurjR y
  have hR : (RingEquiv.ofBijective _ hbijR) (residue R r) =
      residue (R ⧸ I) (algebraMap R (R ⧸ I) r) :=
    ResidueField.map_residue (algebraMap R (R ⧸ I)) r
  have hRh : (RingEquiv.ofBijective _ hbijRh) (residue Rh (algebraMap R Rh r)) =
      residue (Rh ⧸ I.map (algebraMap R Rh))
        (algebraMap Rh (Rh ⧸ I.map (algebraMap R Rh)) (algebraMap R Rh r)) :=
    ResidueField.map_residue (algebraMap Rh (Rh ⧸ I.map (algebraMap R Rh)))
      (algebraMap R Rh r)
  simp only [Algebra.algebraMap_self, RingHom.id_apply, RingEquiv.coe_trans,
    Function.comp_apply, ← hR, RingEquiv.symm_apply_apply, he₀' r, hRh]
  rfl

/-- **A henselization of a quotient of `R` is the corresponding quotient of a henselization of
`R`.** Let `Rh` be a henselization of a local ring `R`, let `A` be a quotient of `R` — a local
ring together with a surjection `R → A` — and let `H` be a henselization of `A`. Then `H` is
isomorphic as a ring to `Rh/I Rh`, for `I` the kernel of `R → A`.

This is Stacks 05WQ followed by the uniqueness of Lemma 08HT: `Rh/I Rh` is a henselization of
`R/I` with respect to `κ(R/I)` by `IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.quotient_of_le_maximalIdeal`, `H`
is one of `R/I` as well once its base is moved along `R/I ≃+* A`
(`IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.of_ringEquiv_base`), and two henselizations with the same
prescribed residue extension are isomorphic over the base, across any universe gap
(`exists_algEquiv_of_isHenselization_independentUniverses`).

The isomorphism is **compatible with the two structure maps**: it carries the class of
`algebraMap R Rh r` to `algebraMap A H (algebraMap R A r)`.  That is not decoration.  Without it
the isomorphism identifies the two rings but says nothing about where a given element of `Rh`
goes, and an element of `Rh` coming from a section on the chart — which is how every geometric
application reaches these rings — then has no known image.  It holds because the comparison of
two henselizations of `R/I` is an isomorphism *of `R/I`-algebras*, which is exactly this
compatibility once the `R/I`-algebra structure on `H` is read through `R/I ≃+* A`.

The three rings are in three independent universes, which is what an application over an
algebraic space needs: `R` is a chart stalk in `Type u` and both `Rh` and `H` are henselian local
rings of the space in `Type (u + 1)`. -/
theorem exists_ringEquiv_quotient_algebraMap_of_isHenselization
    [IsHenselization R (ResidueField R) Rh]
    {A : Type v} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [Algebra R A]
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (algebraMap R A))
    (H : Type x) [CommRing H] [IsLocalRing H] [Algebra A H]
    [IsHenselization A (ResidueField A) H] :
    ∃ e : (Rh ⧸ (RingHom.ker (algebraMap R A)).map (algebraMap R Rh)) ≃+* H,
      ∀ r : R, e (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (algebraMap R Rh r)) =
        algebraMap A H (algebraMap R A r) := by
  have hne : RingHom.ker (algebraMap R A) ≠ ⊤ := by
    rw [Ideal.ne_top_iff_one]
    simpa only [RingHom.mem_ker, map_one] using (one_ne_zero : (1 : A) ≠ 0)
  have hI : RingHom.ker (algebraMap R A) ≤ maximalIdeal R := le_maximalIdeal hne
  let : IsLocalRing (R ⧸ RingHom.ker (algebraMap R A)) :=
    isLocalRing_quotient_of_le_maximalIdeal _ hI
  let : IsLocalRing (Rh ⧸ (RingHom.ker (algebraMap R A)).map (algebraMap R Rh)) :=
    isLocalRing_quotient_of_le_maximalIdeal _
      ((Ideal.map_mono hI).trans (map_maximalIdeal (R := R) (L := ResidueField R)).le)
  have := quotient_of_le_maximalIdeal (R := R) (Rh := Rh) hI
  let σ : R ⧸ RingHom.ker (algebraMap R A) ≃+* A :=
    RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective hsurj
  let : Algebra (R ⧸ RingHom.ker (algebraMap R A)) H :=
    ((algebraMap A H).comp σ.toRingHom).toAlgebra
  have : IsHenselization (R ⧸ RingHom.ker (algebraMap R A))
      (ResidueField (R ⧸ RingHom.ker (algebraMap R A))) H :=
    of_ringEquiv_base σ fun r ↦ rfl
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := exists_algEquiv_of_isHenselization_independentUniverses
    (R ⧸ RingHom.ker (algebraMap R A))
    (Rh ⧸ (RingHom.ker (algebraMap R A)).map (algebraMap R Rh)) H
    (ResidueField (R ⧸ RingHom.ker (algebraMap R A)))
    (ResidueField (R ⧸ RingHom.ker (algebraMap R A))) AlgEquiv.refl
  refine ⟨e.toRingEquiv, fun r ↦ ?_⟩
  have hcomm := e.commutes (Ideal.Quotient.mk (RingHom.ker (algebraMap R A)) r)
  rw [show algebraMap (R ⧸ RingHom.ker (algebraMap R A))
        (Rh ⧸ (RingHom.ker (algebraMap R A)).map (algebraMap R Rh))
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (RingHom.ker (algebraMap R A)) r) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk ((RingHom.ker (algebraMap R A)).map (algebraMap R Rh))
        (algebraMap R Rh r) from Ideal.quotientMap_mk] at hcomm
  exact hcomm

/-- **A henselization of a quotient of `R` is the corresponding quotient of a henselization of
`R`.** This is
`IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.exists_ringEquiv_quotient_algebraMap_of_isHenselization` with the
compatibility of the isomorphism with the two structure maps forgotten. -/
theorem exists_ringEquiv_quotient_of_isHenselization [IsHenselization R (ResidueField R) Rh]
    {A : Type v} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [Algebra R A]
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (algebraMap R A))
    (H : Type x) [CommRing H] [IsLocalRing H] [Algebra A H]
    [IsHenselization A (ResidueField A) H] :
    Nonempty ((Rh ⧸ (RingHom.ker (algebraMap R A)).map (algebraMap R Rh)) ≃+* H) :=
  let ⟨e, _⟩ := exists_ringEquiv_quotient_algebraMap_of_isHenselization (R := R) (Rh := Rh)
    hsurj H
  ⟨e⟩

end IsLocalRing.IsHenselization

end
